-- ACNV2_ONLY C_ADA_ONLY (legacy: no CHOICE of CONTAINING regions sized by an ACN parameter, as 009) KNOWN_FAILURE(Ada,acn-v2,gnata): with -gnata, an encoder postcondition fails: REQUIRED_BITS of an OCTET STRING region around a CHOICE counts the CHOICE's maximum bits, not the region padded to whole octets (Doc2: 17 bits, 3 octets on the wire; Doc3 from an odd bit offset: 47 bits, 6 octets)
-- Issue 132: the OCTET twins of 044. The region around a CHOICE whose alternatives share one size parameter holds the
-- whole CHOICE body padded to whole octets: Doc2 its own index (1 bit) and the contents (16 bits), 3 octets; Doc3
-- aligned alternatives in a region that starts off a byte boundary, up to 6 octets. The decoders bound the region by
-- the CHOICE's own maximum rounded up to octets (3, 6), not by its largest CONTAINING alternative (2 octets), which
-- rejected valid encodings.
TEST-CASE DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN

Val16 ::= SEQUENCE { number INTEGER (0..65535) }

Payload2 ::= CHOICE { value OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Val16), other OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Val16) }
Doc2 ::= SEQUENCE { payload Payload2, trailer INTEGER (0..255) }

Payload3 ::= CHOICE { value OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Val16), other OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Val16) }
Doc3 ::= SEQUENCE { f BOOLEAN, payload Payload3, trailer INTEGER (0..255) }

END

--TCFS   045.acn
